    ENG-2263 Fix advanced node search dropdown menus closing prematurely or not on Tab-away

    Clicking a non-focusable row element (a filter row's label text, a color
    dot) blurs whatever was focused via the browser's default mousedown
    behavior, and since nothing re-focuses afterward, document.body becomes
    the permanent rest state — which SearchDropdown's close-on-blur logic
    misread as focus having left the panel, closing it out from under the
    click. Fixed at the source with onMouseDown preventDefault on each
    interactive row, plus a Tab-away close and toolbar-focus-reclaim so the
    keyboard path back to results isn't lost when a panel closes.

    Also moves node-type filter chips out of the search input (which
    previously rendered and keyboard-navigated them inline) into a dedicated
    tags row below it, and replaces the inline ghost-completion suffix with
    an absolutely-positioned overlay so typing no longer resizes the search
    box.

